  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CBSI-ESC-ESF-CARISECURE II (Strengthened Evidence-Based Decision-Making)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(State Western Hemisphere Regional):  .CariSECURE 2.0 builds upon the successes and lessons learned from CariSECURE, both implemented by the United Nations Development Programme.  CariSECURE 2.0 seeks to reduce youth involvement in crime and violence and strengthen counter TIP efforts in the Caribbean.  It uses a multi-pronged, human rights-based approach designed to improve national capacities to use evidence-based approaches to identify the root causes of youth crime and design policies, strategies, programs, and interventions...While there is a dearth of timely, disaggregated, and comprehensive youth crime data, evidence suggests youth are both the greatest perpetrators and victims of violent crimes in the region.  Moreover, TIP appears to be increasing in prevalence in the Caribbean, most recently linked to the crisis of forced out-migration from Venezuela.  While the paucity of reliable, timely, and comparable data is also present regarding human trafficking, anecdotal evidence suggests that youth are among the most impacted by these crimes...FY 2022 funding will support activities at the regional, national, and community levels in the EC to build the capacity of youth-serving institutions in Barbados, Grenada, and St. Vincent and the Grenadines to better collect, analyze, and use timely, reliable, and standardized disaggregated data for youth crime prevention and response.  Funding will also bolster state capacity to identify, screen, investigate, and prosecute trafficking cases and provide resources and technical support to Barbados, Trinidad and Tobago, Saint Lucia, and Antigua and Barbuda...This activity supports both the Regional Development Cooperation Strategy, relevant ICS, and USAID&apos;s localization priorities through partnering with local and regional partners.  It also works to build the assets, agency, and enabling environment of youth in line with PYD and implements work towards the Youth Policy&apos;s three objectives of access, participation, and system</narrative>
  </description>
